WEBVTT

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:12.260
With summer vacation behind us,
we prepared to start the new semester.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.640
This year marks the Kouka Acting Troupe's
centennial anniversary.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.020
The Kouka Grand Sports Festival
will also be held this year.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.060
The Grand Sports Festival is a huge
fan event held once every ten years.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.270
The actresses of the troupe
are the main focus of the event.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:33.820
Our role is to assist with small tasks
and setting up props and equipment.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.410
We will also be performing
in the halftime show.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:42.790
We're teamed up with the superiors,
so make sure you don't insult them, okay?

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.790
Superiors? What's that?

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.960
Oh, the superiors are the
pros of the pros in the troupe, the o--

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.760
Don't you <i>dare </i>use that three-letter word
starting with "o" and ending in "d"!

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.260
I won't! I was gonna say O-mazing!

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:01.890
Yeah, right! Have you forgotten
the sacred Kouka code?

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.560
What Kouka code?

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:07.900
It's an unspoken rule to never mention
the actresses' real names or ages.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.650
They're supposed to be lovely fairies
that transport us to fantastic worlds.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.780
More precisely,

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:19.740
the superiors are veteran performers that
are not affiliated with any one troupe.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:23.410
They're widely considered to be
the unsung heroes of Kouka.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:23.910
"The Kouka Hierarchy"

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:23.910
They're widely considered to be
the unsung heroes of Kouka.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:27.290
"The Kouka Hierarchy"

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:27.290
They rank high above everyone in Kouka--
even top stars and troupe leads.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:28.380
They rank high above everyone in Kouka--
even top stars and troupe leads.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:33.760
If we make a mistake, it reflects badly
on them, too, so we need to be careful.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.220
Got it?

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.300
Ugh, very well.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.430
Use these to study up.

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:44.810
I shouldn't be surprised, Sugimoto-<i>san</i>!
Nobody loves Kouka like you do!

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.350
It's kinda creepy.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.310
All of them are spectacular,

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.770
but if you watch just one, I recommend
the last Grand Sports Festival.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:53.110
"Celebrating 90 Years Kouka:
The Kouka Grand Sports Festival"
but if you watch just one, I recommend
the last Grand Sports Festival.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.530
I'm so hyped for this, Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.240
Yeah. Thanks.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:31.750
"The Two Juliets"

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:34.000
"The Two Juliets"
It's so good to meet you.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:34.460
"The Two Juliets"
My name is Akiha Ichijou,

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.380
My name is Akiha Ichijou,

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.920
and I'm one of the Superiors.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.840
Let's work hard and put on a great show
for the Centennial's Sports Festival.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.010
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:47.310
That's Ichijou-<i>sama</i>! Even the top stars
regard her with the utmost respect!

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.720
She's got such a regal bearing!

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.600
We'll be forming a marching band during
the cheerleading portion of the event.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.480
We'll play our school anthem,
"Amongst the Cherry Blossoms in the Wind."

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:05.660
Now I really wanna play
the Grilled Potatoes song!

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:06.490
What?

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:10.830
You don't know it? I heard it all the time
in Asakusa. The vendors sing it--

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:16.540
I remember that song. You don't see
many of those traveling vendors nowadays.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.750
Th-That's right, ma'am!

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:23.300
Oh, you don't have to be so formal
with me! Just relax, dear.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.720
She's as lovely as a spring breeze!

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.550
That's Mirei Nohara-<i>san</i>.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:31.470
Both her and Ichijou-<i>san </i>are on the
Board of Directors for the Kouka troupe.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:32.890
Hey, that's her, right?

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:33.810
Yeah!

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:37.610
All the Superiors are so nice!
It's such a relief!

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:42.150
Yeah! With a group like this,
we won't have anything to worry about!

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.070
"First-Year Lockers"

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.150
"First-Year Lockers"

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.150
Hey, guys, we need to redo all of these.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.610
Hey, guys, we need to redo all of these.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:52.250
The second-years said
we cut the tape too thin.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.000
They could've told us what they wanted
before we made them!

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.920
We should've been more worried
about the second-years!

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.380
Stop grumbling. Let's just get it done.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:09.890
My eyes! I <i>can't</i>!

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:11.890
"Spring Troupe, Top <i>Otoko-yaku</i>:
Ryuu Asahina"

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.890
"Summer Troupe, Top <i>Otoko-yaku</i>:
Reo Shiina"

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:15.890
"Autumn Troupe, Top <i>Otoko-yaku</i>:
Keito Mitsuki"

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:17.900
"Winter Troupe, Top <i>Otoko-yaku</i>:
Sei Satomi"

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:21.070
We're so sorry for interrupting!

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:25.610
We're the ones imposing. We saw
your room was open, so we snagged it.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:28.530
You need to get work done, right?
Come on in.

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.830
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.370
All four top stars in one room?!

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.710
Must be a meeting for
the Sports Festival, huh?

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:41.500
Their beauty blinded me, just like Muska
when they destroyed Laputa!

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:44.800
I can't believe you were
able to keep your cool, Sawa.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:46.720
I managed!

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.300
Whoa, do you need a tissue?!

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.350
Satomi-<i>san </i>recognizes us! She's so nice!

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:59.480
That should do it for the torch lighting
and combatant pledge.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.440
Who won last time again?

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:06.700
Summer! And we'll win it again this time,
too! We're going for a streak.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.070
Spring's not giving up without a fight!

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:13.080
We've got a secret weapon
from the JSDF helping us train!

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.290
Wait, you're bringing in Captain Anai?!

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:22.460
Hello, Sachie-<i>san</i>? It's me, Mitsuki.
It's good to hear your voice.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:25.630
Could you help me with something
for the Sports Festival?

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:31.510
Wow, really? Thank you so much!
I'll make sure you get good seats.

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:33.720
Keito-<i>san</i>? Who was that?

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.890
Oh, you know.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:39.190
Just talking to our
favorite sumo instructor.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.020
Sumo instructor?!

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:44.860
Ruri-<i>chan</i>? The other Troupes
are really going all-out...

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:47.940
Wait, for real? Yes!

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.410
The Winter Troupe has three members
who competed in the Track Nationals!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.620
National athletes?!

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:55.990
They're really taking
this seriously, huh...

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.920
Shoot, I forgot the scissors!

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:05.050
I'll go down to the faculty room
and borrow a pair!

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:10.220
Did you see that girl?

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:14.100
Her legs are so long. Maybe that's why
her walk is so elegant.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:18.060
You doing all right, Watanabe?

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.560
Why do you ask?

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:23.940
I mean, you seemed pretty down after
your presentation before summer break.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:30.780
Yeah. It felt like everything I knew
got thrown out the window.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:36.240
But I'm okay now!
I'm back and ready to go!

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:40.660
Is that right?
Well, I'm glad to hear that.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:42.330
Thanks again!

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:47.340
Wow, so you <i>can </i>be nice!

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:49.260
Hey, Satomi.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:51.880
Look at you, acting like
an actual teacher.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.600
I mean, a student from my first class
is top star of her troupe now.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.560
I'd say that means I've
always been an actual teacher.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:01.140
I wish you'd been
this nice to <i>me </i>back then.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.520
I know that girl.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:09.690
You're the one who pushed for her to
get admitted, right? She your favorite?

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.570
Don't be ridiculous.

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:14.990
But you'd agree she's unique
and interesting to have, yeah?

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:17.990
You think she's a contender for top star?

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:21.910
We'll have to see.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:26.580
Today, we'll be rehearsing
our halftime show performance.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:30.340
Ichijou has a Winter show today,
so we'll have to make do without her!

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:31.880
Thank you, ma'am!

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:34.130
One, two, three, four!

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:38.300
Left, right, hit that turn!

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.720
Keep that timing tight!

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:41.770
You, stay on beat!

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:49.570
She's so pretty...

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:53.570
Just a single flourish of her hand
makes her look so regal and elegant!

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:56.200
Let's take a 15-minute break!

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.620
You look kinda worn out, Ai-<i>chan</i>.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:03.660
Really? I'm fine, though.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:05.540
I'm gonna hit the bathroom.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.840
Excuse me, you dropped this!

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:15.930
Oh my, thank you!

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.090
What's your name, hon?

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.890
I'm Chiaki Sawada!

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.140
I, uh...

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:25.520
I absolutely loved your Juliet
way back when!

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.440
Wow, I didn't think people your age
watched those shows!

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:29.900
I did!

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:34.610
And, uh, we just did a scene
from that show, and I got to play Juliet!

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:40.280
And the whole time, I was trying my best
to be as lovely as you were!

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:42.910
Oh, wow, thank you!

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.790
Let's both give it our all
at the Sports Festival, okay?

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:47.040
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:51.710
Did you see that, Chika?!

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:54.920
Keep blabbing and we'll get yelled at
by the second years again.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.800
Oh, right!

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.350
Look how young and energetic they are.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:04.640
You're young, too, Kiyomi-<i>san</i>! Why,
you could be in high school for all I know.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:07.770
You think so? Should I start
wearing a sailor uniform?

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:15.240
Oh, shoot! Akiha told me to tell everyone
we're practicing our march next time.

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:19.030
And most of the students
have already left.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:23.200
Um, uh...

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.830
Oh, right! Juliet!

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:32.040
The first-year who played Juliet! Could I
ask you for your help with something?

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.050
Huh?

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:41.470
Wasn't that...

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:44.680
Chika-<i>chan</i>, right? But she said "Juliet."

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:47.270
She must've thought she was Chiaki-<i>chan</i>.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.940
Mirei-<i>san </i>doesn't know they're twins.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:55.280
Mirei-<i>san </i>is so pretty!

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:58.360
She's a goddess come to Earth,
and Mommy's favorite!

00:10:58.360 --> 00:10:59.610
I like her, too!

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:02.030
Me, too!

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:05.330
When we get older,
we're going to be Kouka actresses.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:08.040
That was all we ever dreamed of.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.460
But the first time we auditioned...

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:12.960
No, no! Why?!

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:15.800
Why did Chika get in and I didn't?!

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:18.920
Chiaki's still up in her room?

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:21.630
She hasn't eaten for three days, either.

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:25.220
I went to check on her, but she's still
crying and won't open the door...

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:27.930
I don't know what to do.

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:31.190
Chiaki, open up.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:33.480
Look, I'm gonna...

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:36.820
I'm gonna turn down my admissions offer.

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:39.440
So let's try again, together.

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:49.200
We'll work really hard
and get in--together.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:52.670
Huh?

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:55.590
I'm sorry, I don't understand...

00:11:55.590 --> 00:12:00.420
I called for you and asked you to help,
but you ignored me and walked away!

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:01.630
I swear, I didn't...

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.640
You looked right at me!

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:05.550
I've done nothing wrong.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:08.930
After all, I'm not Juliet.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:14.100
In our troupe, good manners are more
important than skill in song or dance.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:19.110
You can't put on a lovely performance
if you're not a lovely person!

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:21.280
That's why you speak
when you're spoken to!

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:24.360
I'm not Chiaki. I'm Chika.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:27.330
That's that. Let's begin our reh--

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:30.370
Excuse me! I think there's been a mistake!

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:37.710
There was one show we went to see as kids.

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:41.800
During the revue,
there were two cute bunny rabbits.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:43.630
Look at the bunnies!

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:46.260
They're so cute! They're twins, too!

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:49.180
They're just like us!

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:52.060
We walked at the same pace
with the same footsteps.

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:55.730
We lived in perfect symmetry.

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:59.230
Even if we'd never stand front and center,

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:04.530
we'd stand on opposite sides, creating
a beautiful frame to a performance.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:06.410
I never thought that would change.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:10.700
Watanabe-<i>san </i>explained
the mix-up to the Superiors.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:14.160
As such, the first-year students
will not be penalized.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.960
One, two, three! One, two, three!

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.090
And finish!

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:25.300
We've got three rehearsals left.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:28.430
Be sure to practice on your own
if you feel you need it.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:29.430
Yes, ma'am!

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:39.060
Mirei-<i>san </i>didn't even look at me today.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.940
Ichijou-<i>san </i>didn't say
anything to me, either.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:45.530
Doesn't that mean she doesn't
think it was a big deal?

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:47.200
Really?

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:49.450
Is that <i>really </i>what you think, Chika?

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:52.080
If you've got something to say,
then say it.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.750
I won't.

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:55.960
But if you want me to say it,
then I'll say it.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.460
What the hell does that mean?!

00:13:57.460 --> 00:14:00.710
You're always like this!
You always make me decide!

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.880
Because you always <i>ask </i>me what to do!

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.220
I do not!

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:06.340
You do, too!

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:08.550
I'm always the one letting you
do whatever you want!

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:11.350
Oh, really? Is that how you feel, huh?!

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:15.350
I was stupid to turn down
my first admission offer!

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:19.520
Because there was no guarantee
that you'd ever get in!

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:22.070
That's taking things a little too far...

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:25.320
Fine. I'm running away, then!

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:27.200
Running away?

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:28.150
Go stay in my room.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:30.030
Huh?!

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:33.330
Okay, I'm gonna swap rooms
with Chiaki-<i>chan</i>.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:34.330
Cool.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:40.460
It's so cute! How cool
that you get to room together!

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:42.500
And you like the same stuff!

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:48.170
They said it'd be easier for us to
call home if either of us had issues.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:50.390
You guys are so close!

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:54.390
I'm so jealous. I'm an only child.

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:55.810
Sorry about earlier.

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:58.730
Oh, it's okay!

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:01.100
I'm a horrible person.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:06.360
We've never even fought before.

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:11.200
We knew what we were thinking
without even having to say it.

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:17.200
Or maybe I just imagined we did.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:29.260
Are you sure you don't want to
say something to them yet?

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:32.140
Hmm, well...

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:35.260
I feel terrible for them,
but I have my reasons.

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:43.020
Okay, are the twins still fighting?

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:46.270
I'd like to go back to
my home sweet home...

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:49.110
And the sports festival is almost here.
Are they going to be ready?

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.530
My, you're all still here?

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:53.820
Good afternoon, Ichijou-<i>san</i>!

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:57.080
Aww, you're making pom-poms?
I remember doing that.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:00.250
I came to the Kouka School
after graduating middle school,

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:04.540
and I was also a first year when
they had a Grand Sports Festival.

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:08.340
This one'll be my fourth!

00:16:08.340 --> 00:16:13.220
Sugimoto-<i>san</i>, the numbers are
telling me our lovely fairy's age!

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:15.260
Oh, hey!

00:16:15.260 --> 00:16:19.180
I'm so sorry you had to get involved
because of my mistake.

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:22.640
I love that you have the courage
to stand up for your friends.

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.480
You truly embody the Kouka spirit!

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.440
The Kouka spirit...

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:30.320
And there she goes.

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:33.450
So, what are your dream roles, girls?

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:36.450
Ooh! I want to be Lady Oscar!

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:41.200
I got to see the live show
ten years ago with my grandma!

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:42.250
Ten years ago?

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.670
Yeah!

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.790
We were up on the second floor,

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:50.800
but I could see the real-life Oscar,
and she was so cool!

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:54.180
Really? <i>RoV </i>is such a popular show.

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:55.720
How about you girls?

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:58.100
I've always wanted to
play Death in <i>Elizabeth</i>!

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:02.430
I'd be happy in whatever role I'm offered!

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:05.690
I'd love to sing as Etoile!

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:10.150
I...

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:11.650
I want to be...

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:13.950
A bunny girl.

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:17.950
I saw these bunny girls in a revue once.

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.700
They were really cute.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:23.830
I've always wanted to be
one of those dancing twin bunnies.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:28.590
I always knew.

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:33.590
I knew Chiaki always
regretted my decision.

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:36.720
When admits were announced
our second time around,

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.890
she looked for <i>my </i>number first.

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:45.390
It's there! You're up there!
You made it in!

00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:47.850
And she sobbed.

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:50.400
We did it!

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:53.650
We both got in!

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:02.580
There you are. I've been waiting for you.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:07.420
You're the one who looked at me
and walked away, right?

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.540
I'm sorry.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:12.420
Why didn't you say anything?

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:16.550
Because... I couldn't be Juliet.

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:20.550
I've always loved your
performance as Juliet, too.

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:23.970
But I didn't have the courage
to say I wanted to play her.

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:28.400
Yet my sister got to
play Juliet in her group.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:32.770
Then she was having
so much fun talking with you...

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:35.570
I just started to feel a little jealous.

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:38.320
Then I realized that, even though
we did everything together as twins,

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:42.030
I was always the one who
got the shorter end of the stick.

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:47.540
Then I just kept thinking, and all these
dark thoughts grew and grew...

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:50.670
I'm so sorry I let this happen.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:54.090
Me, too.

00:18:54.090 --> 00:18:57.090
Everyone gets jealous sometimes.

00:18:57.090 --> 00:19:01.300
Especially in Kouka, where the
hierarchy is so harsh on you.

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:04.890
But don't let those
negative emotions control you!

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:10.350
Turn that jealousy into ambition.

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:12.400
I know you'll be okay.

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:17.570
You didn't let your jealousy control you.
You came here to apologize.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:21.160
This bad experience
will only make you stronger.

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.870
You've worked so hard.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:29.460
Yay! You guys aren't fighting anymore!

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:33.710
I'm so glad! Now I get to go back home!

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:34.670
Welcome home.

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:35.710
Thanks!

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:39.510
Oh, yeah, what's the role
<i>you </i>wanna play, Chika-<i>chan</i>?

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:41.590
Do you wanna be the twin bunny, too?

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:43.430
Huh?

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:44.550
Mm-hmm.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:48.890
You guys are <i>already </i>twins,
but you wanna be twins on stage, too!

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:53.270
She figured it out.

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:57.730
Yeah. Sarasa, of all people. Ugh.

00:19:57.730 --> 00:20:02.950
I knew ever since
I didn't get in last year.

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:05.700
Sorry, Chika.

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:09.750
I don't think we can be
exactly the same anymore.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:15.790
We've come upon a fork in the road
much earlier than we expected.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:17.210
But...

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:19.300
Roles for twins?

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:24.720
Well, sisters typically get sent
to different Kouka troupes.

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:30.350
Oh! But if you worked hard
to get yourselves some fans,

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:33.940
at the next Sports Festival,
you can walk out together,

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:36.820
and the crowd will go crazy!

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:42.240
That's right. Our paths will
come together again one day.

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:44.490
Isn't that nice, Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:45.700
Yeah.

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:46.120
"Celebrating 90 Years of Kouka:
The Grand Sports Festival"

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:46.120
Yeah.

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:48.700
"Celebrating 90 Years of Kouka:
The Grand Sports Festival"

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:48.700
I loved all my school sports festivals!

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:49.290
I loved all my school sports festivals!

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:53.870
My grandpa and neighbors
made lots of bentos for us to eat!

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:57.130
It made me happy to know
so many people were rooting for us!

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:59.590
And also a little bit embarrassed.

00:20:59.590 --> 00:21:02.470
Did you like your
sports festivals, Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:21:02.470 --> 00:21:07.180
Well, the last one I went to
was in fourth grade.

00:21:07.180 --> 00:21:12.060
Taichi ordered these huge bentos
that had way too much food.

00:21:12.060 --> 00:21:14.020
It wasn't very fun.

00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:16.600
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:18.690
I totally ruined the moment!

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:23.610
So we'll just have to make sure that
<i>this </i>sports festival is really fun!

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:24.780
Yeah.

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:29.160
Okay, we're rolling!

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:32.410
We're the Superior/Student team,

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:34.750
and we're gonna crush the competition!

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:37.000
"Kouka Acting Troupe's
100th Anniversary Grand Sports Festival!!"

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:37.000
Yeah!

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:40.670
Hey there, Ichijou-<i>san</i>.
Hard at work, I see.

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:42.760
Oh, Shiina!

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:45.510
Do you have a moment?

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:51.560
One of our runners for the relay race
just sprained her ankle.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:53.520
Oh, no! Is she all right?

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:55.140
Yeah, she's fine.

00:21:55.140 --> 00:22:00.730
But management suggested that someone
from the Superiors sub in for her.

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:03.530
Let me think.

00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:06.570
Oh! Since this is our centennial year,

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:10.490
let's have one of our
centennial students sub in instead!

00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:46.960
"Act 10: A Once-in-a-Century Autumn"
